      "message": "Since you bring it up: I\u0027m somewhat resistant to this idea (we can examine things on a case-by-case basis).  But in general, I do think that the \"label-defaults\" section should really be exactly that: the *default* values that are supplied if something else is not.  That\u0027s exactly the old behavior here for tags, it\u0027s just not what you want.  :)\n\nI do agree that it makes sense for tags in particular to behave this way, as it\u0027s a pretty sensible concept to accumulate tags as we increase specificity.\n\nIf we decide that other attributes need more control, then I think we may want to look at override-control or something similar.  We may want to change the name from \"-defaults\" if we don\u0027t think they should be default values (for example, if we think that they should be \"global\" values instead).",
